.\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186265873 :question/problem "Given that\n$X=[\\begin{aligned}-8 & 10 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 8 & 3 \\\\ 9 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]$,\nwhich of the following elementary row operations makes ${a}_{13}=0?$" "Given that\n$X=\\begin{bmatrix}-8 & 10 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 8 & 3 \\\\ 9 & 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}$,\nwhich of the following elementary row operations makes ${a}_{13}=0?$"] [:db/cas 17592186265873 :question/worked-solution "Of the given options, we consider the row operation \n\n$$\n{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(-2){R}_{2}.\n$$\n\nApplying the above row operation, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & =[\\begin{aligned}-8 & 10 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 8 & 3 \\\\ 9 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\,{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(-2)\\cdot {R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-8 & -6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 8 & 3 \\\\ 9 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the required row operation is\n\n$$\n{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(-2){R}_{2}.\n$$" "Of the given options, we consider the row operation \n\n$$\n{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(-2){R}_{2}.\n$$\n\nApplying the above row operation, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & =\\begin{bmatrix}-8 & 10 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 8 & 3 \\\\ 9 & 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\,{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(-2)\\cdot {R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-8 & -6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 8 & 3 \\\\ 9 & 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the required row operation is\n\n$$\n{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(-2){R}_{2}.\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186265874 :question/problem "Given \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}6 & 2 & 4 \\\\ -9 & 1 & -5 \\\\ 8 & 4 & 0\\end{aligned}]$,\nwhich of the following elementary row operations makes ${a}_{32}=0?$" "Given \n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 2 & 4 \\\\ -9 & 1 & -5 \\\\ 8 & 4 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$,\nwhich of the following elementary row operations makes ${a}_{32}=0?$"] [:db/cas 17592186265874 :question/worked-solution "Of the given options, we consider the row operation \n\n$$\n{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1}.\n$$\n\nApplying the above row operation, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned