value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & -7 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 2\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -7 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 2\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186286397 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -3 & -1\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -3 & -1\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186287007 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -10 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -3 & 2\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -10 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -3 & 2\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186287981 :question/problem "Consider the matrix $X,$ given by\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the row operation ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-3{R}_{1}$ on $X?$" "Consider the matrix $X,$ given by\n\n$$\nX=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the row operation ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-3{R}_{1}$ on $X?$"] [:db/cas 17592186287981 :question/worked-solution "The operation ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-3{R}_{1}$ means that we need to add $-3$ times the first row to the second row. \n\nApplying this row operation, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-3)\\cdot {R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 3+(-3)(1) & -1+(-3)(2) & 1+(-3)(1) \\\\ 2 & 3 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -7 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "The operation ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-3{R}_{1}$ means that we need to add $-3$ times the first row to the second row. \n\nApplying this row operation, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-3)\\cdot {R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 3+(-3)(1) & -1+(-3)(2) & 1+(-3)(1) \\\\ 2 & 3 & 2\\end{bmatrix} 