\n$$\n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the following row operations on $B?$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+4{R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186386014 :question/worked-solution "Let's list the required operations:\n\n- The operation ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+4{R}_{1}$ means that we need to add $4$ times the first row to the second row.\n\n- The operation ${R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+{R}_{1}$ means that we need to add $1$ times the first row to the third row.\n\nApplying the operations, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 6 \\\\ -4 & 12 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+4\\cdot {R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 6 \\\\ -4+(4)(1) & 12+(4)(3) & 3+(4)(6) \\\\ -1 & 2 & 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 24 & 27 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\,{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 24 & 27 \\\\ -1+1 & 2+3 & 4+6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 24 & 27 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 10\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "Let's list the required operations:\n\n- The operation ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+4{R}_{1}$ means that we need to add $4$ times the first row to the second row.\n\n- The operation ${R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+{R}_{1}$ means that we need to add $1$ times the first row to the third row.\n\nApplying the operations, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & 6 \\\\ -4 & 12 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+4\\cdot {R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & 6 \\\\ -4+(4)(1) & 12+(4)(3) & 3+(4)(6) \\\\ -1 & 2 & 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 24 & 27 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\,{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 24 & 27 \\\\ -1+1 & 2+3 & 4+6\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 24 & 27 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 10\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186386016 :answer/value